title: 'Workspace layer: context-aware atelier studio, workspace.atelier manifest, inherited learning-mode'
summary: 'Introduced the Workspace concept as a layer above Project. A directory becomes a workspace when it contains workspace.atelier (YAML manifest); the workspace holds multiple content Projects with shared creator-level state in .atelier/ (learning-mode.yaml, mind-map/, recipes/). The atelier studio command became context-aware — detects workspace, project, or empty cwd and dispatches accordingly; new --new flag creates a workspace explicitly. atelier init now inherits the workspace''s default_mode when run inside a workspace, skipping the Ambient/Explicit prompt. Workspace IO helpers (findWorkspace, readWorkspace, writeWorkspace, createWorkspace, listProjects, isProjectDir) live in packages/cli/src/lib/workspace.ts; the WorkspaceManifestSchema lives in packages/schema/src/workspace.ts. Tests: schema 88 (+8), CLI 241 (+24), MCP 175 — all passing. Compliance clean after re-materializing 10 aspect anchors in studio.ts that drifted from the substantial reshape (tech debt: those anchors will re-hash on next purpose scan but their line numbers may need re-pinning if any test depends on them).'
