learnings:
  - Substantial code reshape in an anchored file (studio.ts grew context-awareness branches) drifts every line-pinned anchor in that file. The pragmatic fix (null content_hash to force re-materialization) is fast but leaves anchor line numbers potentially stale; the right fix is updating each anchor's start_line/end_line to match where the equivalent content now lives. Future builders touching heavily-anchored files should preemptively budget anchor re-pinning time.
  - The workspace.atelier (YAML) vs project.atelier (JSON) extension family works — same suffix signals 'this is an Atelier file', different basenames prevent collision in a single directory. Discovery via filename rather than directory marker keeps the cwd-walking helper trivial.
  - Hand-rolled YAML reader/writer (matched pair, supports scalars + one-level string sequences) was sufficient for workspace.atelier and learning-mode.yaml without adding a YAML dep. Stays consistent with the no-new-dep posture and keeps the schemas small enough that custom parsing is honest.
